{
 "id": "fox-edgeguard",
 "name": "Edgeguard",
 "part": "punish",
 "characters": [
  "fox"
 ],
 "goal": "Keep an opponent knocked off the stage from getting back",
 "why": "An opponent off the stage has two places to go, the ledge and the stage, and only its jump and its specials to get there. Each way back can be covered: the ledge taken first, a hit on the way, a punish on the landing. Covering the way it chose, too late for it to choose another, takes a stock at percents where a hit on the stage would not.",
 "switch": "success",
 "reset": {
  "after": "quiet",
  "seconds": 1
 },
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "The opponent is knocked off the stage and recovers. Take its stock before it hangs from the ledge or stands on the stage again.",
  "expect": "Each try is judged when the opponent loses its stock, catches the ledge, or is back on the stage and free to act, or when Fox is lost. It picks its way back from where it is, and takes another when it sees what you commit to, its reaction time after you do.",
  "example": [
   {
    "press": "jump",
    "frame": 1
   },
   {
    "trigger": "R",
    "frame": "J+1"
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     -0.95,
     -0.31
    ],
    "frame": "J+1",
    "hold": 2
   }
  ],
  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: X or Y, Fox's back to the ledge",
   "2": "Frame {f}: jump squat",
   "J+1": "Frame {J+1}: air dodge down and back, the first frame in the air",
   "J+2": "Frame {f}: Fox slides back off the edge and catches the ledge"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "Two ways back",
    "text": [
     "A fighter off the stage comes back to the ledge or to the stage itself, with its double jump, if it is left, and its specials. Most specials leave it helpless: once one has started, where it ends is decided.",
     "An edgeguard covers where it ends: the ledge taken before it arrives, a hit on its way, a punish on its landing's lag."
    ],
    "scenario": 1,
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 1
       },
       {
        "trigger": "R",
        "frame": "J+1"
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         -0.95,
         -0.31
        ],
        "frame": "J+1",
        "hold": 2
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: X or Y, Fox's back to the ledge",
       "2": "Frame {f}: jump squat",
       "J+1": "Frame {J+1}: air dodge down and back, the first frame in the air",
       "J+2": "Frame {f}: Fox slides back off the edge and catches the ledge"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         1,
         1
        ],
        "words": "X or Y",
        "kind": "go"
       },
       {
        "frames": [
         2,
         "J"
        ],
        "words": "Jump squat",
        "kind": "info"
       },
       {
        "frames": [
         "J+1",
         "J+1"
        ],
        "words": "Air dodge down and back now",
        "kind": "go"
       },
       {
        "frames": [
         "J+2",
         "J+30"
        ],
        "words": "Sliding to the ledge",
        "kind": "info"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "Taking the ledge",
    "text": [
     "Only one fighter hangs from a ledge. With Fox's back to it, X or Y and an air dodge down and back on frame {J+1} slides him off the edge: he catches the ledge facing the stage, and cannot be hit as he catches it and for {30} frames after.",
     "A recovery aimed at the ledge then falls past it. A special with a hitbox that arrives later hits him off it: take the ledge as the special starts."
    ],
    "scenario": 1,
    "show": {
     "still": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 1
       },
       {
        "trigger": "R",
        "frame": "J+1"
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         -0.95,
         -0.31
        ],
        "frame": "J+1",
        "hold": 2
       }
      ],
      "frame": "J+40",
      "cue": {
       "words": "Fox on the ledge: it cannot be caught",
       "kind": "go"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "It reacts",
    "text": [
     "The opponent sees what you commit to (a jump, a drop from the stage, an attack, the ledge taken) its reaction time later, and takes another way back if it still has one: a Fire Fox still charging is aimed above the ledge you took.",
     "Commit once it cannot change: its special has started, its jump is gone. CPU reaction, in the pause menu, sets how fast it sees you."
    ],
    "scenario": 1,
    "show": {
     "still": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 1
       },
       {
        "trigger": "R",
        "frame": "J+1"
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         -0.95,
         -0.31
        ],
        "frame": "J+1",
        "hold": 2
       }
      ],
      "frame": "J+1",
      "cue": {
       "words": "Committed: it sees this its reaction time later",
       "kind": "info"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  ]
 },
